{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793372497,"nonce":"0RecmD8b7963GXAi214HUYzak9o=","title":"Sketch: input, surfaces and idleness, for immediate-mode painting","message":"**Today**\n\n`ashui.draw.Sketch` runs `setup` once and `draw(ctx, t, dt)` every frame on the animation scheduler's clock, through `\u003ccanvas sketch\u003e`. `SketchContext` has no input, no way to draw a retained surface, and no way to say nothing changed. No docs or skill-file section.\n\n**Wanted, from RayDE (rayde-00, RayDE git-bug 9c6f60e), in their order of importance**\n\n- A retained, updatable surface a sketch draws: `ctx.surface(s, rect)` over the `\u003csurface\u003e` of 02f829d5e2357bceb45ca7d0a9ec2815959f04309350c0c67cd5464aa48f5d8d. The current frame is a cheap shared object with a generation counter; the renderer skips the upload when the counter is unchanged, and patches dirty rectangles rather than writing everything.\n- Input as an ordered event queue per frame: pointer down, up and move (button, modifiers), wheel, key down and up (repeat), text input and IME composition, focus and blur, resize. Polled helpers (`mouseX`, `keyIsDown`) as sugar on top. A click that begins and ends between two frames must not be lost. Pointer capture while a button is down, and touch, are missing from elements today.\n- Idleness and pacing: a sketch can say nothing changed, so no frame is requested; a target frame rate; a paused or hidden flag so a hidden tab stops drawing.\n- Time on the animation scheduler's clock (already so).\n- Later, Painter parity with OpenFL's Graphics: fills, line styles, curves, gradient and bitmap fills with a matrix, masks and scrollRect clips, blend modes, colour transforms. RayDE will list the gaps.\n\n**Not wanted**\n\nPan, zoom or selection (CanvasKit's job); persistence by key.\n\n**Open**\n\nWhich direction darmie wants for sketches overall; nothing is scheduled.","files":null}]}